I walked through the market.
I got a good smell of spices.
I saw a small shop.
There was a small cardboard board on the table.
The prices are on it.
I looked at the price of cardamom.
The price of cardamom is one hundred and fifty rupees.
The vendor looked at me.
"What do you want?" he asked.
"I need a small packet of cardamom," I said.
"Please give me one packet."
He gave me a packet of cardamom.
I took five hundred rupees from my bag.
I gave it to the vendor.
He took the money and counted the change.
"One hundred and fifty rupees for the cardamom," he said.
"Here is the balance, three hundred and fifty rupees."
He gave me the change.
I put the packet and the money in the bag.
I thanked him.
